#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128925 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Augmented Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/id #uuid "674e7733-7a8e-5804-a867-82c74c583dcc" :question/math-academy-id "e-4687" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n![](images/27/2701e789f5d3f6fc48fda87706add41ccb59c92d5bae4a76e84ac1abfdce6f07.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The first matrix is not in row echelon form since $a_{32} \\neq 0$ (condition II is violated).\n![](images/d8/d8725937a4f5f1cfcd36cbe4871a872187df071b54c15d2e29d9b1e3c5f9b731.svg)\n\n- The second matrix is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](images/5e/5e3142b1ad4bb219db5d5b144e47fe8d1fa8d1f92c300c6f60fc145cf9424900.svg)\n\n- The third matrix is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](images/93/9331fdbede7da49e2dbbc66aac0b3084b1c7acca1ac7e789eded304956a18500.svg)\n\n- The fourth matrix is not in row echelon form since, for example, the leading entry $a_{22}$ lies to the left of the leading entry $a_{13}$ (condition II is violated).\n![](images/76/76e7add6349e0b2fceddf094ac6e3e8cfd0bf1bb43a3fbee0c143b256b81f1c5.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128926 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129114 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d390841-351e-54f5-ad19-90b6ebae5799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/id #uuid "b6e4983b-c695-5944-9637-6d7547dae849" :question/math-academy-id "e-4688" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n![](images/56/564d16a59313514424d24b8c247d8a3516bfa32188292d2cbc7fee7faf2f5744.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n![](images/53/53977f4d27cf659f7d595afc4422b0c3009218fe836615eba5faf8a854124c6b.svg)\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](images/40/40fea7849f3603441671253bb7bc96e56be9bab6a8ddcbc94320238a0e3f529a.svg)\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](images/08/08ed315816def9b28fb3918a2dd103a5008815fc6a07507b64c5c20572b1c88f.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128927 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129115 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe0050b2-b5bc-54a6-aeaf-94cd5d7e5dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Operations That Would Transform a Matrix To Row Echelon Form"}] :question/id #uuid "97237f8e-b317-5c86-86d1-8fd3cc83e66b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4689" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n![](images/aa/aad9e35c3e07e67260a7f3ce96da685be97fab68fe542d262be0ed4f0941f909.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that by replacing $a_{32}$, $a_{42}$, and $a_{43}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n![](images/f8/f89c32a7464b2eeb0f6db6a2c80feef98e8aa24d012b44695e7c7d24b91829ec.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128995 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129176 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "31c3678b-4f00-54d6-bb84-c7718fd622cb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Leading Entries of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "7fd5c01f-c20e-5c47-b8d9-8cfbe634c14d" :question/math-academy-id "e-6166" :question/problem "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n![](images/85/8579b0afd584298a247c38af153d4e69945e73923e9605a168734c9250f3d18a.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows of $A$ are $-1$, $-4$ and $8$, respectively.\n\n![](images/11/11af9a5354d23586af399f9bfade0641e9bb10898068ea825755de5c645e3d9c.svg)\n\nSo, the answer is $-1+(-4)+8=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413823 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129176 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "31c3678b-4f00-54d6-bb84-c7718fd622cb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Leading Entries of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af01445c-3d84-5d24-87a3-64223a7372ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413810} {:answer/id #uuid "ba88dc80-baa7-5c24-9c66-3bc2e7c87798" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413811} {:answer/id #uuid "d4778d8a-14c7-5354-8674-e0b3a10d2f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413813} {:answer/id #uuid "da23471b-f798-5486-86af-971ad557716d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413814} {:answer/id #uuid "de9eacf8-6e58-5082-9700-9ef1eaea5160" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413816}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da23471b-f798-5486-86af-971ad557716d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413814} :answer-field/id #uuid "9abb4bdb-6a2c-505b-9dc2-250a89af5226" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413820}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "43229055-b652-5005-bf91-54dcfc3e2941" :question/math-academy-id "q-129206" :question/problem "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 4 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th rows of $A$ are $-6$, $4$, and $1$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 4 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $-6+4+1=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400422 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129114 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d390841-351e-54f5-ad19-90b6ebae5799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40a5acc6-4f22-572f-9a0b-3eaf9af02343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400424} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca486fb-064c-5b4e-8ab3-1a558d20ebd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400425} {:answer/id #uuid "b98b25bd-05dd-576c-8209-1bbc53b4383c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400426} {:answer/id #uuid "103497c7-00ac-524e-96db-dde3e3e299c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400427} {:answer/id #uuid "a355422c-4d74-55b5-a177-12f7fda4364c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A,$ $B,$ and $C$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400428}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "103497c7-00ac-524e-96db-dde3e3e299c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400427} :answer-field/id #uuid "e24f1ce6-8404-5d4a-83e2-7f5ae99bc979" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400423}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "88771814-b2fc-53f4-914f-2f284d52aece" :question/math-academy-id "q-129222" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry ${a}_{43}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry ${b}_{43}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are **not** in row echelon form."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262994 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Augmented Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06b620f2-8eab-56f7-bf71-ece0313b2c03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259937} {:answer/id #uuid "0e92311e-c0e1-5dd6-a876-0f872e3a96cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260011} {:answer/id #uuid "3255efab-d3ed-5241-8a64-e81d51e7cf3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260328} {:answer/id #uuid "5c74d1ad-b051-5673-95d3-6cf0087523e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260666} {:answer/id #uuid "cbbfc58b-72f2-5768-89a5-a816603a29ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A,$ $B,$ and $C$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbbfc58b-72f2-5768-89a5-a816603a29ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A,$ $B,$ and $C$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261670} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4a71031-b672-5d73-8aa3-dfec74de2c27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b5479435-9835-502a-bd24-1f955706f0c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-129228" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 9 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 9 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ are in row echelon form."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413825 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Augmented Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bcbaf3a-7d79-5c34-9970-8e30a0164f3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A,$ $B,$ and $C$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413798} {:answer/id #uuid "12f4ffe3-c54b-5dec-af7e-f3eb29c5efac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413800} {:answer/id #uuid "3fd4fdcb-52a1-577b-9cee-a9fa9d18334b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413805} {:answer/id #uuid "42122353-59f4-5dee-9867-47f69bf794e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413806} {:answer/id #uuid "e9c227b1-80fa-5ed1-8fcb-7bbadbc92d9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fd4fdcb-52a1-577b-9cee-a9fa9d18334b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413805} :answer-field/id #uuid "848d2bf5-7181-5403-afac-d10425ef5d8c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a0f43991-a609-584a-a820-e263b283da38" :question/math-academy-id "q-129230" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -9 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{33}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -9 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ and $C$ are in row echelon form."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265725 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129115 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe0050b2-b5bc-54a6-aeaf-94cd5d7e5dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Operations That Would Transform a Matrix To Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0624289a-8dfc-5c15-af8f-ba1cb4c34aba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${a}_{31}$, ${a}_{32}$ and ${a}_{33}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263054} {:answer/id #uuid "5ff2eaee-3fb7-558b-904e-b1aa73f1dfaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${a}_{31}$, ${a}_{32}$ and ${a}_{43}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263829} {:answer/id #uuid "af33b68d-5796-591c-9b65-1f0810f7895a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${a}_{31}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264513} {:answer/id #uuid "cc67339b-098a-579e-9a59-6b83f013016d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${a}_{31}$ and ${a}_{32}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264789} {:answer/id #uuid "f9d9608c-c7fe-5edb-90bd-370db5125284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${a}_{31}$, ${a}_{43}$ and ${a}_{44}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ff2eaee-3fb7-558b-904e-b1aa73f1dfaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${a}_{31}$, ${a}_{32}$ and ${a}_{43}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263829} :answer-field/id #uuid "021f4039-528b-5a31-a6af-7977fed20985" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265253}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4da5d683-7056-5520-8077-4c10803e9f98" :question/math-academy-id "q-129424" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that by replacing ${a}_{31}$, ${a}_{32}$ and ${a}_{43}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\,⟶\\,[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe other options will not give us a matrix in row echelon form."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413824 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129114 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d390841-351e-54f5-ad19-90b6ebae5799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18db0a49-6e70-5b48-904f-fb9b5f8f1167" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413801} {:answer/id #uuid "1d8d25d8-fe04-53ff-b342-7ebac143d4d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413802} {:answer/id #uuid "1dc8f4a4-b6d6-5c99-bf78-b1f7a4d93a23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413803} {:answer/id #uuid "521a920f-2f8c-531a-965b-1cdb14e91dd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413807} {:answer/id #uuid "bf0253c3-f269-5021-82aa-caf40ced2760" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "521a920f-2f8c-531a-965b-1cdb14e91dd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413807} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f91971d-c20c-5a76-a12b-2827ef0652b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413818}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "72e836b6-2968-5b2e-8666-6c15080ad3e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-42005" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{32}\\ne 0$ (condition  II is violated). \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since ${b}_{21}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is in row echelon form."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413822 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129115 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe0050b2-b5bc-54a6-aeaf-94cd5d7e5dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Operations That Would Transform a Matrix To Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e03e0f4-f6d8-5e5e-be1b-2065040084b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${a}_{43}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413799} {:answer/id #uuid "2231485a-d292-515f-b51b-91f31ecd0efe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${a}_{32}$, ${a}_{43}$ and ${a}_